\title{glmmplanr: Two-Dimensional Sample Size Planning for Crossed Binary GLMMs}
\description{
Plans numbers of participants and items for studies with one binary response per trial, including correct or incorrect answers in forced-choice tasks and yes or no judgments. Uses crossed generalized linear mixed models (GLMMs) and explanatory item response models in behavioral science, psycholinguistics, and language assessment (Westfall et al. (2014) \doi{10.1037/xge0000014}; De Boeck et al. (2011) \doi{10.18637/jss.v039.i12}). Generates balanced Latin-square, between-within, incomplete-block, and testlet-nested designs with configurable factor contrasts; numerically inverts marginal cell probabilities and guessing probabilities in multiple-alternative forced-choice tasks into conditional GLMM parameters by Gaussian quadrature; evaluates power, accuracy in parameter estimation through interval widths, exclusion of a region of practical equivalence, convergence, coverage, magnitude and sign errors, and Monte Carlo uncertainty intervals (Morris et al. (2019) \doi{10.1002/sim.8086}); and identifies non-dominated Pareto-optimal (N_subj x N_item) designs using Universal Kriging monotone Gaussian process surrogates and multi-stage parallel 'C++' estimation. Supports both random-item and fixed-bank Rasch parameter recovery planning.
}
